{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 128, :comments ["<b>Therefore I have conformed</b> — the yod in place of alef, as in כי אשרוני בנות, and likewise תתיימרו, from the paradigm יתאמרו, all workers of iniquity." "<b>And the sense of פקודי כל</b> — that all the statutes include every person of understanding, and this word comes in the manner of: כל בכורי כל."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 119, :notes {0 "The cited forms appear to be garbled or abbreviated; translated hyper-literally as they stand. The standard paradigm form is יתאמר, and 'all workers of iniquity' (כל פועלי און) seems to be a truncated citation, possibly from Psalms 59:3 (כל פועלי און) or similar."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:40:51.254583243Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}